a group of magical horses wild  youngsters and made a pretty penny for  franchise originator Hasbro - so when it  was announced in 2010 that both the toys  and the cartoon were due for a reboots  people didn't know what would happen we  think the biggest surprise was that my  little  so often seen as a thing for girls would  attract a range of male fans known as  bronies these young and not so young men  helped blow apart gender stereotypes  let's be honest people who remember the  original phenomenon had absolutely no  idea that this was going to happen but  the show's main themes of working  together using kindness to defeat evil  and the power of friendship reached out  to a whole new audience it didn't  exactly hurt matters that the new show  entitled My Little Pony Friendship is  Magic had a radically new animation  style either gone were the soft gentle  cartoons of the 1980s they were replaced  with hard edged comic-book style  psychedelic artwork these coupled with  an increase in humor and excitement  meant that the new show was able to  absolutely knock the socks off the  original that said we'll always have a  soft spot for the first series three  scooby-doo mystery Incorporated  scooby-doo where are you is one of the  best-loved and most iconic TV cartoons  of all time the stories of teenagers  Fred Velma Daphne Shaggy and their Great  Dane  scooby-doo were smash hits across the  globe it was yet another classic cartoon  from hanna-barbera and did let a whole  lot of spin-offs while it's cool if you  like the follow up shows we don't think  they quite match the 1960s original  until scooby-doo mystery Incorporated  hit our screens it was in 2010 that  Warner Brothers announced the new show  it told the story of how they got  together and started solving mysteries  what was so invigorating about the new  show was that it simultaneously took the  show back to its root and into new  places acknowledging that a franchise  that started more than 40 years ago  would have fans all ages it tipped its  hat to a range of pop-culture references  viewers would have spotted nods to other  beloved shows like Wacky Races and the  1960s Batman they would have also seen  homage 'as to legendary rock acts like  The Velvet Underground and the Ramones -  and they would have got away with it if  it wasn't for you pesky kids  but while we'd love the original Scooby  Doo we think that scooby-doo mystery  Incorporated is even better than the  original two extreme Ghostbusters most  of the show's we are  today are reboots of the original  cartoons in some cases they are the  first time the classic show has been  updated for a new audience in others  they are the best in a pretty long line  of remakes but this next one is a little  bit different  you see back in the 1980s it wasn't  uncommon for a live-action movie to turn  into a smash hit kids cartoon and the  biggest in this sub-genre was the Real  Ghostbusters taking the 1984 classic  movie it animated the main characters  made Slimer an icon and kept Ray Parker  jr.  stone-cold legendary theme tune for a  lot of the kids born in the 80s Peter  Venkman Egon Spengler ray Stantz  and winston zeddemore were cartoons  before they were flesh and blood but  everything changes and in 1997 there was  a new generation of ghostbusters for  fans to enjoy Egon stayed and served as  a mentor for Kylie Eduardo Garrett and  Roland's joining them were original  Ghostbusters secretary Jeanine and of  course Slimer the program had a grittier  more streetwise animation style this was  matched by a zeitgeist II grunge punk  version of the classic theme tune the  show dealt with big topics tackling  racism prejudice and diversity the shock  to the system it provided paved the way  for the 2016 all-female movie remake  we're still fans of the Real  Ghostbusters but extreme Ghostbusters is  we think and under lists classic one the  Powerpuff Girls when it comes to  rebooting a much-loved classic series  timing can be everything if you do it  too soon people will shrug their  shoulders and wonder why you've done it  if you leave it too long it makes your  job harder fans who love taking the show  to their hearts and won't countenance  the idea of remaking it so we think the  gap between the original Powerpuff Girls  and its reboot 14 years is perfect  there's enough of a break for people to  get nostalgic but it's not too long that  viewers ideas of what a show is get  fixed for kids growing up around the  turn of the millennium the stories of  Blossom Bubbles and Buttercup were  thrilling and iconic when the Cartoon  Network announced it was rebooting the  show in 2016 lots of us were really  excited not only were the Powerpuff  Girls back they were better than ever  they still had their superpowers  bestowed on them by professor utonium  still  Chemical X on them while in the lab but  the shows were now more character-driven  and there was even just a dash of social  commentary with the addition of the  fourth Powerpuff Girl Bliss the show had  25% more so we think the new Powerpuff  Girls is even better than the original  but what do you think what's your  favorite cartoon reboot and which  classic cartoon would you like to see  rebooted tell us in the comments that  wraps up our 5 cartoon reboots that are  way better than the original if you  liked it check out 10 cartoons that look  different in other countries thanks for  watching and don't forget to subscribe  to the things  [Music]

